// serial-connection phase, Task 5: `conn.send` on a never-opened
// connection is a contract violation (a bug, not weather -- see
// conn.cla's own header comment and the design spec's "Error principle"),
// so rtConnSendText panics "connection not open" rather than staging a
// `failed` event.
//
// Host-only pinning, same layout convention as stringat_oor.cla (.cla +
// .err + .behavior; discovered by internal/selfhost/behavior_test.go's
// testdata/runerr glob). NOT yet exercised by T1 (behavior_test.go lives
// in internal/selfhost, which scripts/test-task.sh explicitly excludes).
//
// Task 4 (binary-files phase) STALE-SNAPSHOT ARTIFACT: TestBehaviorGoldens
// bootstraps from the COMMITTED clarusc/clarusc.c snapshot, which predates
// Task 4's runtime ABI change (`connection` is now an int VALUE -- the
// global's own slot+1, not a bare compile-time slot constant -- and
// rtConn* take that 1-based handle, conn.cla's own `h == 0` nil check).
// The frozen snapshot still EMITS the old 0-based slot constant (0, for
// this program's only connection global), which the new runtime decodes
// as `h == 0` -- nil -- so THIS fixture, compiled by the stale snapshot,
// currently observes "use of nil connection" instead of its originally
// intended "connection not open". This is expected to revert to
// "connection not open" once a later task regenerates clarusc.c from
// current source (current-source codegen assigns this global slot+1 = 1,
// a real non-nil handle, so `conn.send` reaches the not-open check
// again) -- see lower.cla's lowConnMethod/lowGlobalVarDecl and
// runtime/clarus/conn.cla's rtConnSendText for the current-source
// behavior this fixture will exercise again at that point.
var conn: connection

on App.startCLI(args: list of string) {
    conn.send("x")
}
